MTCC (Modern Tiny C Compiler)
-----------------------------

MTCC is a Zig-built, single-file frontend around a vendored copy of TinyCC.
The unmodified-as-possible TinyCC sources, build system, and docs live in
`src/`; everything at the repo root is MTCC-specific.

Build:

    ./src/configure --cc="zig cc"
    make mtcc
    make test-mtcc

Run a C file directly with `mtcc hello.c`. Use `mtcc run`, `mtcc build`,
`mtcc lint`, or `mtcc tcc` for explicit command routing. Zig 0.16.0 is used by
the release workflow; Zig is not required at runtime.

To build plain TinyCC itself (no Zig involved), see `src/README`.

See `AGENTS.md` for engineering standards.
